{"study_accession":"PRJNA767116","secondary_study_accession":"SRP341794","title":"diabetes mellitus with tuberculosis RNA sequencing","description":"Due to the rising prevalence and adverse effects of diabetes mellitus (DM), especially in countries where tuberculosis (TB) is most endemic, the DM-TB comorbidity has been recognized as a major obstacle towards achieving the World Host immune responses affected by diabetes can lead to increased susceptibility, severity and poor treatment outcomes in DM-TB patients, and the underlying mechanisms have not yet been fully elucidated. This study aimed to identify key immunological and cellular components that contribute to increased morbidity and mortality in DM-TB cases. We performed RNA-Seq of total RNA isolated from peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) from 3 TB, 3 DM, and 3 DM-TB patients and healthy controls, and analyzed differential expression, pathway enrichment, and clustering of differentially-expressed genes (DEGs) to identify biological pathways altered specifically in DM-TB patients.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":12,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN21876994","study_accession":"PRJNA767116","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","description":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","sex":"male","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-10-02","attributes":[["isolate","Health donor"],["age","41"],["biomaterial_provider","Shenzhen Center for Chronic Disease Control and Prevention"],["sex","male"],["tissue","PBMC"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR16379655","experiment_accession":"SRX12657092","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"PolyA","instrument_model":"HiSeq X Ten","read_count":23697800,"base_count":6710025328,"first_public":"2023-10-02","experiment_title":"HiSeq X Ten sequencing: Health donor"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN21876996","study_accession":"PRJNA767116","blood_class":"pbmc",